1
00:00:01,660 --> 00:00:04,030
Narrator: Previously
on "Final Space"...

2
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:05,900
After five years of jail time
alone on a prison ship,

3
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:09,170
our hero Gary made not one,
but two friends.

4
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:12,240
One is a planet-killer, the
other a deadly bounty hunter.

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:14,880
And both of them lead right
back to the Lord Commander,

6
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:17,010
who's kind of a jerk-face.
Well, guess what?!

7
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:19,820
We're off to a great start,
so buckle up those butt cheeks,

8
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:22,590
'cause things are
about to get heavy.

9
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:30,230
H.U.E.: Gary, you have eight
minutes of oxygen left.

10
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:32,730
H.U.E., if you had
eight minutes to live

11
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:35,730
and you could do anything
you wanted, what would you do?

12
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,200
Facticulating.
Ahh.

13
00:00:38,230 --> 00:00:41,670
I would transfer my A.I.
into a corporeal being

14
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:44,770
and go see Paris.

15
00:00:44,810 --> 00:00:49,510
Oh, that's lame!
I mean, wow. Super...cool.

16
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:51,550
What would you do,
Gary?

17
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,050
Absolutely anything.

18
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:55,250
And I mean anything with Quinn.

19
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:57,920
I mean, we could watch
"Space Drive" for all I care.

20
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:01,620
I'm sorry things
turned out this way.

21
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:03,060
Crap happens.

22
00:01:03,090 --> 00:01:12,940
♪♪

23
00:01:12,970 --> 00:01:23,280
♪♪

24
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:31,120
♪♪

25
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:38,560
♪♪

26
00:01:38,590 --> 00:01:41,630
KVN: ♪ Holes, holes, holes,
holes, cover up these holes ♪

27
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,130
♪ Plug these holes

28
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:44,800
♪ Holes, holes, holes, holes

29
00:01:44,830 --> 00:01:46,400
♪ Nothing but holes,
nothing but holes ♪

30
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:49,100
♪ Nothing but holes,
but holes, but holes ♪

31
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:51,140
♪ Holes, holes, holes, holes,
cover up these holes ♪

32
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:52,740
♪ Plug these holes,
holes, holes ♪

33
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:53,980
♪ Nothing but holes

34
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:55,240
♪ Holes, holes, holes

35
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,450
♪ But holes

36
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,780
♪ Plug these -- plug

37
00:01:57,810 --> 00:01:59,780
♪ Plug these holes,
holes ♪

38
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:02,820
♪ Holes, holes, holes, holes

39
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:06,160
Quinn, it's me, Gary. Things
have been great on my end.

40
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:08,660
I made what I believe to be
a potential new friend.

41
00:02:08,690 --> 00:02:10,160
Yes, he boarded
the ship to kill me

42
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,660
and take my little
green ball friend,

43
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:16,530
but Avocato is one
great card player.

44
00:02:16,570 --> 00:02:18,870
Any more cards and I
will shoot myself.

45
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:21,340
I'm gonna shoot you
if you don't play cards.

46
00:02:21,370 --> 00:02:23,670
-I'll let you shoot me.
-Um, oh -- real--

47
00:02:23,710 --> 00:02:25,310
Well, then I'm gonna
shoot myself!

48
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:26,540
What? Why?

49
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,340
Frickin' figure it out.
Figure it out.

50
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,350
And our newest member
is this little guy!

51
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:32,520
His name's Mooncake.

52
00:02:32,550 --> 00:02:33,520
Ooh!

53
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:35,020
Everyone loves him.

54
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:36,650
That little
green snot-ball

55
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:38,550
is a planet-destroying
super-weapon

56
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:39,860
that's gonna
get us killed.

57
00:02:39,890 --> 00:02:43,530
You, sir, just stepped
over the line.

58
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,030
Mooncake has feelings.

59
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:47,500
And you just peed all over them
with your cat whiz.

60
00:02:47,530 --> 00:02:50,870
Gary: Yep. Things have been
going pretty great.

61
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:52,340
Get back to me.
No rush.

62
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,540
It's just I haven't talked
to a human lady person

63
00:02:54,570 --> 00:02:57,370
in, like, five years.

64
00:02:57,410 --> 00:03:00,710
Well, yours forever.
Thunder bandit!

65
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:01,810
Message sent.

66
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,580
I crushed it...again!

67
00:03:03,610 --> 00:03:05,380
[ Breathes deeply ]

68
00:03:05,410 --> 00:03:06,650
[ Device beeps ]

69
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,650
Quinn.

70
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,220
Hey, Quinn,
it's Tribor.

71
00:03:09,250 --> 00:03:11,320
An Infinity Guard ship
has crashed.

72
00:03:11,350 --> 00:03:13,760
How did it crash,
we don't know.

73
00:03:13,790 --> 00:03:15,560
We need you on the scene.

74
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:17,490
On my way.

75
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:20,430
Ha. Oh, mama. Oh, boy.

76
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:21,730
Oh!

77
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,770
H.U.E.:
Unauthorized scan detected.

78
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:26,200
[ Alarm blaring ]

79
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,270
What ya doing, Gary?

80
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:32,940
Gotcha.
Lord Commander -- agh!

81
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,080
Hmm.

82
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:36,950
Set course
for Tera Con Prime.

83
00:03:41,950 --> 00:03:43,090
[ Electricity crackling ]

84
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,620
What the heck
is this thing?

85
00:03:44,650 --> 00:03:47,220
A Ventrexian
stealth probe -- Turk.

86
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:48,760
Of course, Turk.

87
00:03:48,790 --> 00:03:49,960
Who the hell is Turk?

88
00:03:49,990 --> 00:03:51,760
A bounty hunter --
like me.

89
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:53,360
If he scanned Mooncake,

90
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,530
he'll be on his way back
to the Lord Commander

91
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,100
to gather reinforcements.
-Mm-hmm.

92
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:58,870
-Unless we stop him first.
-Mm-hmm.

93
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,200
It we don't, they will
capture Mooncake.

94
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,770
-Mnh-mnh.
-And take us to the Dark Zone.

95
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:04,770
Mnh-mnh.
And torture us
with zargon slugs.

96
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:06,310
Mnh-mnh.

97
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:09,280
Or we're gonna suffer pain
and anguish for eternity.

98
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:11,450
Oh.
And the only way
to stop them is with salt.

99
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:15,280
Oh.
And there's no salt
in the Dark Zone.

100
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,490
Hmm.

101
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:20,890
Sounds like I got these
buttery buns into a hot vise.

102
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,060
How do I stop them?
-You don't.

103
00:04:23,090 --> 00:04:24,660
But together,
we've got a shot.

104
00:04:24,690 --> 00:04:27,130
Get me out of these cuffs,
and we'll go after him.

105
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,260
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, cowboy!

106
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,400
You tried to kill me.

107
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:33,670
If you want me to trust you,
first we clasp.

108
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:34,970
I'm not doing that.

109
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,140
Oh, yes, you will.
You will do that.

110
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:39,310
We've enjoyed recreational
cards together.

111
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:40,810
This is the next step.

112
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,650
A hand-to-hand bond
that forges

113
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:45,280
the completion
of a newfound trust.

114
00:04:45,310 --> 00:04:47,850
We don't have to get balls
to the wind naked, do we?

115
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:51,020
Tradition demands yes.
But you're lucky.

116
00:04:51,050 --> 00:04:53,020
I'm more of a progressive.

117
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:55,920
Trust mode engaged.

118
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:58,130
It's been five years
since I've been off this ship!

119
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:02,000
I am pumped for adventure!
Let's get this guy!

120
00:05:02,030 --> 00:05:03,270
H.U.E., open the airlock.

121
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:05,000
H.U.E.:
You are a prisoner.

122
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:06,770
How will I know
you won't run?

123
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:07,840
-I got nowhere to g--
-Inject.

124
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,200
Ow!
What the freak was that?!

125
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:12,010
If you are not back aboard
this ship in five hours,

126
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,480
your brain will go
into convulsive spasms

127
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:16,350
and then explode.

128
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:18,180
Let's go!

129
00:05:18,210 --> 00:05:19,520
Shouldn't we take Mooncake?

130
00:05:19,550 --> 00:05:22,150
It's too dangerous.
Make haste, make haste!

131
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:23,350
I'll miss you, bud.
Be good.

132
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:25,650
And don't whiz on
any of my stuff.

133
00:05:25,690 --> 00:05:31,860
♪♪

134
00:05:31,890 --> 00:05:38,170
♪♪

135
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,540
Oh, oh!
Street meat!

136
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:42,140
They got street meat, Avocato!

137
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:43,870
-Focus.
-Okay, I'm focused.

138
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:46,210
Gary: All right,
we're getting Turk.

139
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:54,520
For the galaxy, for eternity,
for Lord Commander.

140
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:58,750
You're lucky that we
even made it here.

141
00:05:58,790 --> 00:06:00,720
They don't take kindly
to Homo sapiens.

142
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,990
Now let's go to tier 24

143
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:03,990
and get you
identification papers.

144
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:06,430
-Ha! I don't need papers.
-Or they'll liquify you.

145
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:09,400
Did you just say liquify?
Or was that a brain spasm?

146
00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:12,100
Is it happening?
Oh, my crap, it's happening.

147
00:06:12,130 --> 00:06:15,900
Or we'll kill you.

148
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:17,240
Gary, stay close.

149
00:06:17,270 --> 00:06:20,080
Right, don't worry.
I'm not going anywhere.

150
00:06:20,110 --> 00:06:22,380
-Gary!
-Getting some street meat!

151
00:06:22,410 --> 00:06:25,580
Identification papers!

152
00:06:25,610 --> 00:06:28,780
Um, I must have
left them in, um...

153
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:31,450
We got a runner.

154
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:36,390
Maybe we should
get some papers.

155
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:37,360
Mm-hmm.

156
00:06:37,390 --> 00:06:40,760
KVN: Welcome
to the hangar bay!

157
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,130
But I call it
the tiger's nest.

158
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,700
And I bet
you're wondering why.

159
00:06:43,730 --> 00:06:45,430
Well, okay,
I'll tell you.

160
00:06:45,470 --> 00:06:46,870
Whoo!

161
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,440
Uh, excuse me,
can I help you?

162
00:06:48,470 --> 00:06:52,440
Uh, hello.
Run away! Run away!

163
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:03,220
Ahh. Avocato,
it's so good to see you.

164
00:07:03,250 --> 00:07:06,620
What brings you to my
little shop of doo-dads?

165
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:07,760
Cut the crap, Clarence!

166
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:09,630
Yeah,
cut the crap, Clarence.

167
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,630
-We need papers.
-That's right, papers.

168
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:14,460
Well,
papers are not cheap.

169
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:15,800
-[ Growls ]
-Oh!

170
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:17,970
Neither is your life,
and I saved that.

171
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,640
Yes, right,
I suppose you did.

172
00:07:19,670 --> 00:07:22,910
But this is the last time.
Your papers are easy.

173
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:24,810
But this primate...
-Hey!

174
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,340
...is gonna be much
more difficult.

175
00:07:26,370 --> 00:07:30,250
Get your finger
out of my tummy.

176
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,480
Ooh! It speaks.

177
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,350
I guess you can
train anything.

178
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:37,290
I'll touch you any time
I wish, primate!

179
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,620
Hmm.

180
00:07:38,650 --> 00:07:41,320
Yes, no, not that one.
Hold on a second.

181
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,690
Down here at the bottom,
possibly.

182
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:45,090
Oh, yes, here we go.

183
00:07:45,130 --> 00:07:46,600
Skin of a dead Hooblat.

184
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,660
I have to get
in this thing?

185
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:51,470
It's like a slippery
pita pocket.

186
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,340
You want to be liquefied
and have Mooncake

187
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:54,670
and the Galaxy 1 destroyed?

188
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:57,010
No, h-- How the hell
do you know that?

189
00:07:57,040 --> 00:08:00,140
It's everywhere.
It's all anyone's talking about.

190
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:01,280
Huh.

191
00:08:01,310 --> 00:08:03,150
Both: Get in the skin!

192
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:04,680
For Mooncake.

193
00:08:04,710 --> 00:08:07,380
Oh, my God,
it's so warm!

194
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:09,690
Oh, it's -- and wet!
Oh.

195
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:12,520
It actually kind of
feels kind of nice,

196
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:15,190
like a pair of warm,
wet house slippers.

197
00:08:19,190 --> 00:08:20,530
It doesn't make any sense.

198
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:23,200
I know. It doesn't
make any sense.

199
00:08:23,230 --> 00:08:24,570
I wish there was sense.

200
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,400
Where did
all the sense go?

201
00:08:26,430 --> 00:08:28,700
I don't get it.
It's an Imperium T3.

202
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:30,640
These things don't crash.

203
00:08:30,670 --> 00:08:32,980
They don't crash,
you're right.

204
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:34,710
It doesn't
make any sense.

205
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:35,980
Why would it crash?

206
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:38,810
Tribor,
look me in the eye.

207
00:08:38,850 --> 00:08:40,980
Now shut up.
-I should shut up.

208
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:43,550
Why do I keep talking?
-Are you reading this?

209
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:45,350
The gravitational
constant is shifting.

210
00:08:45,390 --> 00:08:47,560
I am seeing it.
I am!

211
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:49,020
A disturbance this strong

212
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:52,330
can literally tear
the universe apart.

213
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,730
H.U.E.: Intruder alert.

214
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:56,930
Initiating anti-gravity
countermeasures.

215
00:08:56,970 --> 00:09:03,110
♪♪

216
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:06,440
Sames, initiate
defense sequence.

217
00:09:06,470 --> 00:09:12,080
♪♪

218
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:15,850
Anyway, I'm kind of in charge
of security around here,

219
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:18,050
which brings me
to a big ask.

220
00:09:18,090 --> 00:09:20,220
Could you go out there
and get me a cookie?

221
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:22,020
-Chocli.
-Score!

222
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:24,630
All right, I'll stay here
and guard the fort.

223
00:09:27,430 --> 00:09:28,800
How do I look?
Be honest.

224
00:09:28,830 --> 00:09:30,600
-I'd give you a 2.
-Just a 2?

225
00:09:30,630 --> 00:09:32,130
Get my hair done
or something, you know.

226
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:33,240
How about no?

227
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:34,600
No, seriously,
I could get highlights.

228
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,100
I could get ombre hair,
you know?

229
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:37,270
I can't believe it.

230
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:39,140
Believe it, because this
ombre hair is happening.

231
00:09:39,170 --> 00:09:41,780
-No. Turk!
-Oh, crap, it is Turk.

232
00:09:41,810 --> 00:09:43,710
What are you looking at?
What are you looking at?

233
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,110
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

234
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:47,120
Hmm.

235
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:49,950
[ Choking ]

236
00:09:49,990 --> 00:09:51,250
Thought you could
rat us out, huh?

237
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:54,890
How the hell are you,
you old bag?

238
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:58,590
Okay.
That just hurts.

239
00:09:58,630 --> 00:09:59,900
Avocato!

240
00:09:59,930 --> 00:10:01,300
No!

241
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:02,930
Give me one reason
I don't kill you right now

242
00:10:02,970 --> 00:10:04,570
for leaving me to die
on that ship!

243
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:07,140
Because I know
where your son is.

244
00:10:07,170 --> 00:10:10,240
My son?
Where? Where is he?

245
00:10:10,270 --> 00:10:12,570
Holding cell 43.

246
00:10:12,610 --> 00:10:14,740
He's...he's here?

247
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,580
Now let me go.

248
00:10:16,610 --> 00:10:18,810
I'll let you go.

249
00:10:18,850 --> 00:10:20,650
I'll let you go
to Hell.

250
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:29,790
[ Screaming ]

251
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:30,960
[ Screaming stops ]

252
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:36,500
[ Screaming resumes ]

253
00:10:36,530 --> 00:10:38,830
I'm coming, Avocato.

254
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,840
Melanie Duinger, level 4.

255
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:45,540
Melanie Du--
what -- what?!

256
00:10:45,570 --> 00:10:47,680
Aah! Oh!

257
00:10:47,710 --> 00:10:49,950
-Mommy!
-Mommy!

258
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:53,450
-You're back!
-I sure am!

259
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,480
Oh, no!
-Melanie!

260
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:59,890
Oh, they told us
you were dead!

261
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,060
Oh!

262
00:11:01,090 --> 00:11:05,330
Everything with
your sister was a mistake.

263
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:08,700
Oh, my crap.

264
00:11:23,410 --> 00:11:25,480
Sit tight.

265
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:26,720
I can't hear you.

266
00:11:26,750 --> 00:11:28,850
I messed up.
I messed up bad!

267
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,890
But I'm not gonna
leave you here. I promise.

268
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,160
I'll do
whatever it takes.

269
00:11:33,190 --> 00:11:37,260
No, Dad! Dad, run!
It's a trap!

270
00:11:37,290 --> 00:11:40,730
Dad, watch out!

271
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:43,900
Dad, Dad, Dad, no!

272
00:11:43,930 --> 00:11:46,770
Take him
to the Lord Commander.

273
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,910
I love Mommy more!

274
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:53,280
No, I love Mommy more!

275
00:11:53,310 --> 00:11:54,740
Okay, just, uh -- stop --

276
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:57,280
keep -- stop tugging
too hard, babies.

277
00:11:57,310 --> 00:11:59,550
[ All scream ]

278
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:02,280
Melanie?!
Oh, God!

279
00:12:04,050 --> 00:12:07,060
So you probably have
a few questions.

280
00:12:07,090 --> 00:12:09,860
Get out of here,
you maniac!

281
00:12:09,890 --> 00:12:12,390
[ All crying ]

282
00:12:12,430 --> 00:12:13,830
Hyah!

283
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:17,270
Huh!

284
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:22,100
Avocato!

285
00:12:23,270 --> 00:12:24,810
Whew.

286
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,940
The clasp of friends.

287
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,380
Only two hours till my brain
shoots out of my eyes.

288
00:12:31,410 --> 00:12:32,750
I gotta move fast.

289
00:12:35,650 --> 00:12:38,450
[ Indistinct conversations ]

290
00:12:38,490 --> 00:12:39,960
Sir,
there's an emergency.

291
00:12:39,990 --> 00:12:42,660
We need to ground all Infinity
Guard cruisers immediately.

292
00:12:42,690 --> 00:12:44,090
What?!
Not again, Quinn.

293
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:46,090
There's a cosmic
disaster taking place.

294
00:12:46,130 --> 00:12:47,760
We need to find out
what's causing --

295
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,230
Quinn, shut up!

296
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:51,330
The Imperium T3 crashed
because of human error.

297
00:12:51,370 --> 00:12:55,140
Yeah? Tell that to science.
You're an idiot.

298
00:12:55,170 --> 00:12:57,810
-Back me up, Captain.
-Time to leave, Quinn.

299
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:00,580
Okay. The Captain
is also an idiot.

300
00:13:00,610 --> 00:13:02,110
Lieutenant?

301
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:03,310
[ Clicking ]

302
00:13:03,350 --> 00:13:05,450
You're all idiots!
Idiots, idiots!

303
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:08,150
Are you idiots?
Why would you all be idiots?

304
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:10,250
I think
you're all very smart.

305
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:11,020
[ Yelling ]

306
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:12,620
Well, I gotta go.

307
00:13:12,650 --> 00:13:16,160
H.U.E.: Stop! Stop,
or I will be forced to...

308
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:25,000
Manual override of AI.
H.U.E. disable...

309
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:31,940
♪♪

310
00:13:31,970 --> 00:13:33,210
Avocato.

311
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,710
We had a deal.

312
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:37,780
You promised me E-351

313
00:13:37,810 --> 00:13:41,850
and you failed...
again.

314
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:44,150
Trust me,
I can do this.

315
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:45,490
I'm close.

316
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:49,690
Ooh! Ooh, hurray.
When will it be mine?

317
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:52,390
Wait, are you hiding it on you?
Is this a game?

318
00:13:52,430 --> 00:13:55,560
I love games.
-I don't have it.

319
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:58,170
But I can get you
the man who does.

320
00:13:58,200 --> 00:13:59,700
His name is Gary.

321
00:13:59,730 --> 00:14:03,410
I get you him,
you give me back my son.

322
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:06,070
No deal.

323
00:14:06,110 --> 00:14:08,040
There you are!

324
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,380
What a day I've had, man.

325
00:14:09,410 --> 00:14:11,350
I think I destroyed
a family.

326
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:14,520
Oh. So how about
we get out of here?

327
00:14:14,550 --> 00:14:18,250
You must be the Gary.

328
00:14:18,290 --> 00:14:20,260
Okay.
Actually, it's just Gary.

329
00:14:20,290 --> 00:14:21,890
-The Gary.
-Just Gary.

330
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,730
You know, just --
just -- there's no...

331
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:27,030
Where's this "the"
coming from?

332
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:30,670
Well, this has been great.
But, Avocato, run!

333
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:34,070
I haven't
introduced myself.

334
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:37,740
I am the Lord Commander.

335
00:14:37,770 --> 00:14:40,210
Oh, is that you?
That's fantastic.

336
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,880
But we really gotta -- Avocato!

337
00:14:41,910 --> 00:14:47,250
You have something of mine,
and I want it.

338
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:49,580
Come here, the Gary.

339
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:52,520
What is going on?
Oh, God!

340
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:54,520
Okay, this is --
it's nice to be wanted.

341
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,790
But this is --
this is too much want.

342
00:14:56,820 --> 00:15:00,800
Are you going to
give me E-351,

343
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:04,400
or should I tear you
limb from limb?

344
00:15:04,430 --> 00:15:06,400
Avocato, a little help.

345
00:15:06,430 --> 00:15:08,400
Oh! Oh!

346
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:11,270
[ Groaning ]

347
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:13,440
Avocato,
the clasp of friends!

348
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,580
Please, man! Avocato!

349
00:15:15,610 --> 00:15:17,210
[ Sighs ]

350
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,980
[ Groaning ]

351
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:23,490
Friend mode!
Engaged!

352
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:24,890
Friend?

353
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:27,490
He was just
betraying you.

354
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:30,630
Untrue. We clasped hands.
Right, bro?

355
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:34,560
I was desperate, man.
I was trying to save my son.

356
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:37,270
Aah! Oh, my God!

357
00:15:39,870 --> 00:15:42,740
You idiot!
That's my freakin' arm!

358
00:15:42,770 --> 00:15:44,410
You just ripped the thing off!

359
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,840
Aah!

360
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:49,310
Oh, my God!
Oh, what the freak?!

361
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:51,710
I'm spraying all my blood!

362
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:57,690
I am going to murder
your face off!

363
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,320
I will murder
your face on!

364
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,420
That doesn't make
any sense!

365
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,430
-Run!
-Oh!

366
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:05,160
Come on!

367
00:16:05,190 --> 00:16:07,200
After them!

368
00:16:07,230 --> 00:16:09,460
-Oh, there's so many stairs!
-Quit talking, you idiot!

369
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,500
Why are there
so many stairs?!

370
00:16:13,370 --> 00:16:16,770
Gary,
I can't leave my son.

371
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,010
Oh, we're going,
all right --

372
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:21,140
and fast -- before
my brain explodes!

373
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:24,050
[ Gunfire ]

374
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,850
We're not gonna make it
back to the transporter.

375
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:28,880
Looks like
we got a new ride.

376
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:32,320
Okay, not ideal,
but still a ride.

377
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:33,890
Oh, come on!

378
00:16:34,490 --> 00:16:37,360
I don't even know
what that is.

379
00:16:37,390 --> 00:16:40,030
Crap it hard!

380
00:16:42,230 --> 00:16:44,170
We jump to the catwalk.
-Are you insane?

381
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:47,570
No, I'm super insane.
Ha ha ha!

382
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:52,740
[ Both screaming ]

383
00:16:59,350 --> 00:17:00,850
Attaboys.

384
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:02,680
I'll need that suit back.

385
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:05,250
We're falling!
Oh, my gosh!

386
00:17:05,290 --> 00:17:08,060
Wahhh!

387
00:17:08,090 --> 00:17:11,230
Oh, my God, David, kids!
It's me, your mother!

388
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:12,990
[ All scream ]

389
00:17:13,030 --> 00:17:15,830
No, my arm!

390
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:17,930
I forgot my arm
back up there!

391
00:17:19,970 --> 00:17:23,210
This is no good!
H.U.E., pick up, pick up!

392
00:17:25,810 --> 00:17:26,770
Are those what I think
they are?

393
00:17:26,810 --> 00:17:28,010
Viper turrets.

394
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:29,880
Okay, that's not good.
That's not good!

395
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,910
Quick, hug me.
-Hug you?

396
00:17:32,950 --> 00:17:34,380
-Hug a friend!
-What?!

397
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:35,620
Hug me!

398
00:17:35,650 --> 00:17:38,720
Oh, we're hugging!

399
00:17:41,390 --> 00:17:45,990
H.U.E.?
H.U.E., come in!

400
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,360
Quinn.

401
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,700
Quinn,
where are you going?

402
00:17:50,730 --> 00:17:52,030
To the first Hawk
I can jack.

403
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:53,440
Something
big is happening,

404
00:17:53,470 --> 00:17:55,440
and I'm not waiting
while command sits around,

405
00:17:55,470 --> 00:17:56,940
twiddling their wieners.

406
00:17:56,970 --> 00:17:58,240
Maybe I can't stop it,

407
00:17:58,270 --> 00:17:59,570
but I'm going to find out
what it is.

408
00:17:59,610 --> 00:18:01,110
Cover for me.

409
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:07,750
♪♪

410
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:10,550
Why would they be
twiddling their wieners?

411
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:12,650
Why?

412
00:18:12,690 --> 00:18:14,660
Wait, I'm gonna
need six cookies.

413
00:18:14,690 --> 00:18:16,620
And another one.
So seven -- eight cookies.

414
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:18,230
Wait, nine cookies!

415
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:21,900
Ah, I guess I better
give him a hand.

416
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:26,430
KVN, you're going to have
to save the Galaxy 1

417
00:18:26,470 --> 00:18:27,600
someday.

418
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,970
Inside of you
now is the answer.

419
00:18:31,770 --> 00:18:35,110
Hey, Mooncake.
My name is Nightfall.

420
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:38,010
Don't let Gary die
because of you.

421
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:44,150
Gary: H.U.E.!
Come in, H.U.E.!

422
00:18:44,190 --> 00:18:46,020
H.U.E.:
Arrr-- yes, Gary?

423
00:18:46,050 --> 00:18:47,760
What the crap,
H.U.E.?!

424
00:18:47,790 --> 00:18:49,290
I've been calling you.

425
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:51,760
We need you to
scoop us up A.S.A.P.P.!

426
00:18:51,790 --> 00:18:54,360
On my way, Gary.

427
00:18:59,830 --> 00:19:03,270
He-e-e-ey, Gary,
your arm is gone.

428
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:05,170
Oh, my gosh.
Is it? Really?

429
00:19:05,210 --> 00:19:06,440
I know my arm is gone,

430
00:19:06,470 --> 00:19:08,010
you decaying pile
of fecal matter!

431
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:09,810
Now get this thing
out of my head, H.U.E.

432
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:12,110
H.U.E.: Oh. It was never going
to explode, Gary.

433
00:19:12,150 --> 00:19:14,120
That's just
my sense of humor.

434
00:19:14,150 --> 00:19:16,620
You make one joke
in five years,

435
00:19:16,650 --> 00:19:18,790
and that
is the one you tell?

436
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:22,790
Timing...is everything, Gary.

437
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:24,990
Hmm.

438
00:19:25,030 --> 00:19:26,130
Whoo.

439
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,730
[ Clank! ]

440
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:29,730
My arm! My arm!

441
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:31,470
Interesting.

442
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:34,870
We can surgically implant
an animatronic arm on you.

443
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:37,040
Gary, while you were
gone, an intruder --

444
00:19:37,070 --> 00:19:38,740
Shut your face hole, KVN.
Didn't you just hear the news?

445
00:19:38,770 --> 00:19:40,380
I'm getting a robot arm.

446
00:19:40,410 --> 00:19:43,250
But someone will need to
perform the procedure, Gary.

447
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:45,910
Avocato: I'll do it.

448
00:19:49,020 --> 00:19:51,190
You?

449
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:54,390
Create temporary
arterial shunt.

450
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:57,860
I thought we were gonna be
like super friends, man.

451
00:19:57,890 --> 00:20:00,400
I've had one mission for
the past three years, Gary,

452
00:20:00,430 --> 00:20:02,260
and that is
to find my son.

453
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:05,100
You should have told me.
We did the clasp of friends.

454
00:20:05,130 --> 00:20:07,100
I would have straight-up
helped you get your son back.

455
00:20:07,130 --> 00:20:09,670
What? Why?
You barely know me.

456
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:12,240
Yo, we played nine hours
of cards together.

457
00:20:12,270 --> 00:20:15,280
That might not mean something
to you, but it did to me.

458
00:20:15,310 --> 00:20:16,940
Expose bone for plating.

459
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:18,410
Friends help each other
through thick

460
00:20:18,450 --> 00:20:20,950
and thin and thinner
and nothing.

461
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:22,620
I have nothing
to give in return.

462
00:20:22,650 --> 00:20:25,450
Yeah, you do, yo.
Your friendship, yo.

463
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:26,850
I've been stuck here
for so long

464
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:28,190
with just
freakin' robots.

465
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:31,530
Look robot, robot, robot,
robot, robot, robot!

466
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:32,560
Freakin' robot.

467
00:20:32,590 --> 00:20:34,060
That's the refrigerator,
Gary.

468
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,960
Really? Because
I've had some serious,

469
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,600
dark conversations
with that thing.

470
00:20:37,630 --> 00:20:40,740
I knows
everything about me.

471
00:20:40,770 --> 00:20:43,870
Keep your mouth shut,
you lying robot!

472
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:47,680
Micro-vascular transplant
coverage complete.

473
00:20:52,010 --> 00:20:54,750
It's an unconventional way
to start a friendship, but --

474
00:20:54,780 --> 00:20:55,980
Hmm?
-Shh!

475
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:59,820
No words.
Only clasps.

476
00:21:01,790 --> 00:21:03,390
Bro, you being real
this time?

477
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:04,760
As real as it gets,
baby.

478
00:21:04,790 --> 00:21:07,460
Then I promise you,
we will get your son back.

479
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:08,730
And keep Mooncake safe.

480
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:10,100
And murder
that guy's face off.

481
00:21:10,130 --> 00:21:11,570
I don't think
that's a great idea.

482
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:13,970
Real raw friendship
mode engaged.

483
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,400
Ooh!

484
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:26,280
♪♪

485
00:21:26,310 --> 00:21:34,260
♪♪

486
00:21:34,290 --> 00:21:40,060
Where you're going,
your father will never find you.
